    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dooley Poynton Auctioneers are delighted to present to the market this five-bedroom detached coastal bungalow, ideally situated within the mature and highly sought after Blainroe Estate in Co. Wicklow. This property is surrounded by open fields and offers an excellent combination of coastal living and recreational amenities, all within easy reach of Wicklow Town. The accommodation comprises a spacious living room, kitchen/dining room, conservatory, five bedrooms, walk-in wardrobe, two en-suites, a family bathroom and a utility room. Outside, the property boasts a large rear garden and patio area, offering an abundance of space in which to relax, entertain or enjoy the tranquil setting. The garden is particularly appealing to those with an interest in growing their own produce as there is a greenhouse and vegetable patch readily available. Blainroe Estate has an excellent range of leisure and recreational facilities. Residents have access to three tennis courts and a padel court, while the estate's Pavilion being the heart of its social life, hosting many activities and events throughout the year. These range from movie and games nights, table tennis, art and fitness classes during the quieter months to a busy programme of summer social events. The location is particularly well suited to those seeking an active coastal lifestyle. Blainroe Golf Club is situated directly across the road with access to its private beach for any residents of the estate. The Pin High driving range is also close by, while Blainroe Beach, Magheramore Beach and Silver Strand are all within easy reach. The renowned Brittas Bay is approximately 10 minutes away. Wicklow Town is just a five-minute drive, providing convenient access to an excellent selection of shops, restaurants, schools and all other amenities it has to offer as well as being within easy reach of the M11 motorway, making it an excellent option for commuters. This five-bedroom bungalow truly has something for everyone and offers a wonderful opportunity to create a beautiful family home in one of Wicklow’s most desirable locations"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Living Room (5.38.m x 4.09m) \r\nThis bright and spacious living room benefits from an abundance of natural light, with French doors opening our into the garden. The room is centered around an attractive stone feature fireplace with a solid fuel stove and slate hearth, creating a warm and inviting focal point. This room also features recessed ceiling lighting and solid wood flooring throughout. A doorway leads directly into the adjoining kitchen as well as the conservatory, providing a natural flow between the living spaces.\r\n\r\nConservatory (2.15m x 5.20m)\r\nThis light infused conservatory offers a calm haven to relax. featuring a pitched glass roof and French doors open out into the private courtyard, creating a seamless connection between indoor and outdoor living.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room (5.85m x 4.29m) \r\nThis open plan kitchen/dining room enjoys pleasant views overlooking the rear garden. The space features an excellent range of high and low kitchen units, generous countertop space and a stainless-steel double sink unit. The kitchen also features integrated Whirlpool appliances such as a four ringed hob, integrated microwave and Oven. This room has recessed ceiling lighting and tiled flooring throughout. French doors provide direct access to the rear patio and garden area.\r\n\r\nUtility Room (1.70m x 4.20m)\r\nThis spacious utility room features both a Candy washing machine and separate dryer and provides ample storage with built in cabinetry. A door leads to a private car port.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom (1.97m x 1.93m)\r\nThis family bathroom features floor to ceiling tiling, a wash hand basin with a shaving mirror, chrome towel rail, , w/c and a bathtub with a Triton T90Z electric shower. \r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom (3.01m x 4.20m) \r\nThis master bedroom overlooks private courtyard. and features built-in floor to ceiling wardrobes, recessed lighting and solid wood flooring. This space also boasts an ensuite bathroom. \r\nEnsuite (3.01m x 1.11m)\r\nThe en-suite features a pump shower, chrome towel rail, w/c and a vanity unit with a wash hand basin. This space also features floor to ceiling tiling. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (.42m x 4.14m) and Bedroom 3 (2.43m x 4.30m)\r\nThese bright east facing bedrooms feature pendant lighting and timber flooring throughout.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 (3.45m x 3.12m)\r\nThis bedroom enjoys a sunny aspect, overlooking the picturesque rear garden. This space features pendant lighting, a built-in wardrobe and timber flooring throughout. This room also benefits having a wash hand basin. \r\n\r\nBedroom 5 (4.20m x 3.12m)\r\nThis bedroom is flooded with natural light overlooking the rear garden and features a Velux window. This room boasts a walk in wardrobe and ensuite. \r\n\r\nWalk in Wardrobe (2.13m x 0.96m)\r\nThis walk in wardrobe provides ample space with floor to ceiling built in shelves. \r\n\r\nEnsuite (2.13m x 1.76m)\r\nThe en-suite features a spacious pump shower, chrome towel rail, w/c and a vanity unit with a wash hand basin. This space also features floor to ceiling tiling and a shaving mirror. \r\n\r\nRear Garden\r\nThe property boasts a large rear garden, offering a wonderful sense of space and privacy bordered by mature trees and fields . A paved patio area provides the perfect setting for alfresco dining and outdoor entertaining, while the garden also features a greenhouse and an established vegetable patch including cabbaged, carrots, aubergines, lettuce and more. This large garden provides an idyllic outdoor space in which to relax, entertain or just enjoy the peaceful surroundings. \r\n\r\nServices: \r\n•\tGroup Water Scheme\r\n•\tGroup Sewage Scheme\r\n•\tOil Fired Central Heating\r\n•\tOutdoor water taps\r\n•\tOutdoor lighting\r\n•\tOutdoor Socket\r\n•\tBER: C  BER NO:107530909\r\n•\tEnergy Performance Indicator: 175.35kWh/m2/yr\r\n•\tManagement Company: Blainroe Estate Management.\r\n•\tManagement fees €2300 PA"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tFive bedroom, detached private bungalow.\r\n•\tRear and side garden with a greenhouse.\r\n•\tSituated only a 5-minute drive from Wicklow Town Centre.\r\n•\tSituated in a mature development of bungalows.\r\n•\tA number of leisure activities are available within the development.\r\n•\tPrivate gated courtyard.\r\n•\tPrivate gated parking bay.\r\n•\tAccess to the private Blainroe Beach.\r\n•\tBlainroe Golf Club opposite the development."
      },
